  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read notes/decisions.md D-219 and review section 2.1 rows for AssignWorkFollowOnStep.tsx (:249, :257, :307, :328, :336).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the optional navigationService to the CreateRecordWizard config type and pass it from CreateRecordWizard.tsx (~441-466) to AssignWorkFollowOnStep.</step>
    <step order="3">In AssignWorkFollowOnStep render Matter Type, Practice Area, Assigned Attorney, Assigned Paralegal and Assigned Outside Counsel with DataverseLookupField, keeping the existing search callbacks as onSearch; the two contact fields pass the active-contacts filter; keep "Assign to me".</step>
    <step order="4">Pass the navigationService the Matter, Project, Event and Report Card wizards already receive into their config (Report Card ~402-426 passes it to the step directly).</step>
    <step order="5">Add tests and run the dev check.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-179-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the side pane opens behind the wizard dialog on dev, STOP and escalate rather than adding a z-index or yieldToSidePane workaround (review section 4 risk 5).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/types.ts:46, 311 (navigationService exists only inside associateToStep and existingRecordPicker).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: one optional field on the existing config, read by the existing step; no new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it the Assign Work step has no way to open the side pane, so F-R4-2 (owner UAT round 4) stays failed in four wizards.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Assigned Attorney opens the side pane in Create Project, Next steps → Assign Work">
      <steps>
        <step>Open Create Project, Next steps → Assign Work in the Console (in-app) on dev</step>
        <step>Reach the step with Assigned Attorney; click its Select button</step>
        <step>Pick a record; then reopen and cancel</step>
        <step>Switch the Console to dark mode and repeat</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Dataverse side pane opens above the wizard; the pick shows as a chip; cancel keeps the prior value; all values already typed in the wizard are kept; no white surfaces in dark mode; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Assigned Outside Counsel opens the side pane in Create Matter, Next steps → Assign Work">
      <steps>
        <step>Open Create Matter, Next steps → Assign Work in the Console (in-app) on dev</step>
        <step>Reach the step with Assigned Outside Counsel; click its Select button</step>
        <step>Pick a record; then reopen and cancel</step>
        <step>Switch the Console to dark mode and repeat</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Dataverse side pane opens above the wizard; the pick shows as a chip; cancel keeps the prior value; all values already typed in the wizard are kept; no white surfaces in dark mode; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/steps/AssignWorkFollowOnStep.tsx</output>
