  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a navigationService, then Matter Type, Practice Area, Assigned Attorney, Assigned Paralegal and Assigned Outside Counsel render no inline search input and open the pane for their tables (the two person fields: contact with the active-contacts filter; Outside Counsel: sprk_organization, no filter).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a pick in each field, then the picked ids and names reach onFinish (the work assignment create) unchanged from today's shape (assignedAttorneyId/Name, assignedParalegalId/Name, assignedOutsideCounselId/Name).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Assign to me" still fills Assigned Attorney.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given no navigationService, the step renders exactly as today; the existing AssignWorkFollowOnStep.assignToMe test passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of the four wizards passes its navigationService into the config (one test per wizard asserting the captured config has it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dev check (Console in-app wizard AND one code-page dialog wizard): the side pane opens ABOVE the wizard; after a pick and after a cancel the wizard is usable and keeps every value already entered; light and dark themed (review section 4 risk 5).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (closed set, every task): no new lookup component, no new email form, no change to the behaviour of the inline `LookupField.tsx`, and no `Xrm` import added to any component file (the host injects `INavigationService`; ADR-012).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; tsc clean; no new ESLint errors in touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>D-219 removed the owner-question gates (2026-11-12). Source: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md (Fable review 2026-11-12) and UAT round 4 findings F-R4-2 / F-R4-3 (notes/uat-v4-log.md).</notes>
